-**Pitfalls:**
-*   **Quadrilateral Subdivision:** Do not subdivide quadrilaterals formed by stitching. Subdivision is not unique and causes cracks in 3D isosurface extraction [S1].
-*   **Vertex Generation:** Do not generate new vertices. Use only existing grid vertices to maintain compatibility with dual grid structures [S1].
-*   **Consistency:** Ensure that edge cases (where only one coarse endpoint is refined) use the same tessellation logic as other edge cases to avoid topological inconsistencies [S1].
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Quadrilateral Subdivision:** Quadrilaterals formed by stitching must not be subdivided. Subdivision is not unique and causes cracks in 3D isosurface extraction [S1].
+*   **Mixed Refinement:** Cases where only one endpoint of a coarse edge is refined must be handled consistently with other edge cases to avoid topological errors [S1].
+*   **Vertex Promotion:** When a coarse vertex is refined, it must be promoted to an edge segment to maintain consistent tessellation logic [S1].
 
